WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.390 --> 00:00:02.640
- [Lauren] Every time I take my eagle out

00:00:02.640 --> 00:00:05.190
I get butterflies in my stomach.

00:00:05.190 --> 00:00:08.180
It's this dichotomy between
a heavy bird on your fist

00:00:08.180 --> 00:00:11.203
that just instantly
becomes lighter than air.

00:00:14.270 --> 00:00:17.713
You get to cultivate a
really unique relationship.

00:00:18.830 --> 00:00:21.330
There are very few people flying
eagles in the United States

00:00:21.330 --> 00:00:24.350
and of that only a handful of women.

00:00:24.350 --> 00:00:26.110
But my very good friend Jamaica

00:00:26.110 --> 00:00:29.160
is beginning her journey
into eagle falconry.

00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:31.770
- [Jamaica] The ability
to be mentored by a woman,

00:00:31.770 --> 00:00:33.920
I thought that that was something unique,

00:00:33.920 --> 00:00:36.020
that I shouldn't pass up that opportunity.

00:00:51.947 --> 00:00:54.310
- [Lauren] Falconry is the
ancient art and tradition

00:00:54.310 --> 00:00:55.970
of using a trained bird of prey

00:00:55.970 --> 00:00:58.863
to hunt its natural quarry in the wild.

00:01:00.140 --> 00:01:01.870
I spent a lot of time in Mongolia

00:01:01.870 --> 00:01:04.210
apprenticing under Kazakh eagle hunters.

00:01:04.210 --> 00:01:06.963
When I started I felt pretty out of place.

00:01:07.980 --> 00:01:10.660
Because I didn't have
that hunting experience,

00:01:10.660 --> 00:01:11.493
and I was a girl,

00:01:11.493 --> 00:01:16.120
it made me really fortify
my passion and persevere.

00:01:16.120 --> 00:01:17.970
Because it was hard in the beginning.

00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:21.920
- [Jamaica] I've admired
her from the very beginning.

00:01:21.920 --> 00:01:25.450
Her journey into falconry
was different than most.

00:01:25.450 --> 00:01:29.170
The gumption she had as a
teenager to go to Mongolia

00:01:29.170 --> 00:01:31.710
and learn about eagle falconry,

00:01:31.710 --> 00:01:32.710
that's a rare thing.

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:36.510
Here boy,

00:01:36.510 --> 00:01:37.343
atta boy.

00:01:38.780 --> 00:01:42.360
A little over a year ago
I got a call from a friend

00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:44.920
who had found an eagle
standing in the road

00:01:44.920 --> 00:01:46.340
about a mile from my house.

00:01:46.340 --> 00:01:48.423
It was close to death.

00:01:49.290 --> 00:01:51.200
So I took it to the vet that afternoon

00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:53.943
and participated in rescuing that eagle.

00:01:55.140 --> 00:01:58.130
Falconry is pretty much
the only way at this point

00:01:58.130 --> 00:02:00.570
that we know for sure allows that eagle

00:02:00.570 --> 00:02:03.030
a reasonable chance at survival.

00:02:03.030 --> 00:02:05.270
By helping them through that period

00:02:05.270 --> 00:02:07.520
where they're learning
how to catch things.

00:02:07.520 --> 00:02:10.730
I made it my life's mission
to get an eagle permit

00:02:10.730 --> 00:02:15.130
and acquire an eagle though
an established rehab program

00:02:15.130 --> 00:02:16.693
that works with falconers.

00:02:17.530 --> 00:02:19.950
There's a lot of knowledge
involved in falconry.

00:02:19.950 --> 00:02:21.950
There's also a lot of ways to do it wrong.

00:02:21.950 --> 00:02:25.000
It's really not necessarily instinctive.

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:27.750
I would not want to
get into eagle falconry

00:02:27.750 --> 00:02:30.670
without a good mentor to contact.

00:02:30.670 --> 00:02:33.670
Knowing that Lauren was
available to be a mentor to me

00:02:33.670 --> 00:02:37.433
was a huge part of being
willing to make that decision.

00:02:38.750 --> 00:02:41.020
- [Lauren] To get inside
the mind of an eagle

00:02:41.020 --> 00:02:42.680
the first time is,

00:02:42.680 --> 00:02:44.943
it can be a difficult experience.

00:02:46.610 --> 00:02:48.330
You just have to find your bearings

00:02:48.330 --> 00:02:50.310
and understand where
an eagle's coming from

00:02:50.310 --> 00:02:54.080
in order to create a good,
fit, confident hunting eagle.

00:02:54.080 --> 00:02:56.430
So essentially that's what
I'm helping Jamaica do.

00:02:56.430 --> 00:02:58.500
When you find someone
that has that passion

00:02:58.500 --> 00:03:00.160
and is willing to share it with you,

00:03:00.160 --> 00:03:02.113
it's really a special thing.

00:03:03.570 --> 00:03:04.670
- [Jamaica] The bond that you develop

00:03:04.670 --> 00:03:07.680
with someone who gives of you their time

00:03:07.680 --> 00:03:09.220
the way that Lauren is giving to me,

00:03:09.220 --> 00:03:11.330
it will be something
I'll treasure forever.

00:03:11.330 --> 00:03:14.493
And hopefully, someday, I'll
pass that on to somebody else.

